<title>CHINA: Bank of East Asia interim net up 21.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of East Asia interim net up 21.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   78	 vs 65</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    25.5     vs 21.3</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil	vs 28.27 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    1,030.33 vs 846.92</p>
<p>    Company name		 Bank of East Asia Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  Aug 25-29</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   Sept 26</p>
<p>NOTE - Bank of East Asia is a local commercial bank. The comparative  earnings per share and interim dividend figures have been adjusted  for the one-for-five bonus issue made in April 1997.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
